   "source": [
    "#### Create variables needed for analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "To support our exporatory analysis, we derive additional variables from the existing dataset that will help us examine patterns related to our hypotheses.\n",
    "\n",
    "First, we convert the \"death\" column to a datetime format so that we can extract time-based features. This allows us to create a death_month variable, which enables us to analyze potential seasonal patterns in homicide deaths. Since our hypothesis suggests that homicide incidents may increase during the summer months due to increased social activity and outdoor interaction, examining deaths by months helps us explore this relationship."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "homicide_clean[\"death\"] = pd.to_datetime(homicide_clean[\"death\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "homicide_clean[\"death_month\"] = homicide_clean[\"death\"].dt.month\n",
    "\n",
    "non_homicide_clean[\"death\"] = pd.to_datetime(non_homicide_clean[\"death\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
